          "citation": "503 U.S. 347 (1992)",
          "court": "Supreme Court of the United States",
          "year": 1992,
          "date_decided": "1992-03-25",
          "holding": "The Supreme Court reversed, holding that the 'reasonable efforts' requirement of the Adoption Assistance and Child Welfare Act, 42 U.S.C. § 671(a)(15), is enforceable by the Secretary through the state-plan approval process but confers no privately enforceable right under § 1983 and creates no implied private cause of action.",
          "relevance": "Real, controlling authority for this node: federal child-welfare performance conditions are enforced administratively by HHS through funding, not by private suit.",
          "quote": "We conclude that 42 U. S. C. § 671 (a)(15) neither confers an enforceable private right on its beneficiaries nor creates an implied cause of action on their behalf",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/112712/suter-v-artist-m/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 112712
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Momox-Caselis v. Donohue",
          "citation": "987 F.3d 835 (9th Cir. 2021)",
          "court": "United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit",
          "year": 2021,
          "date_decided": "2021-02-03",
          "holding": "The Ninth Circuit affirmed summary judgment for the county and its officials in a suit over a foster child's death, holding the family failed to prove deliberate indifference under the special-relationship exception or to establish a Monell claim given the county's licensing and training policies.",
          "relevance": "Shows that documented licensing and training compliance defeats a claim of systemic constitutional failure.",
          "quote": "The \"special relationship\" exception applies when there is a custodial relationship between the plaintiff and the State, such that the State assumes some responsibility for the plaintiff's safety and well-being.",
